      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T11:21:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But how do you check for an unlinked file today? \nWe can do that with d_unlinked(). \n\u003e You don\u0027t want to get a path for an unlinked file, do you?\nWe need a \"clear\" path for unlinked files too. The problem is that \"(deleted)\" suffix doesn\u0027t guarantee that a file is unlinked. A file may contain this suffix in its path. So we have to call d_unlinked() in any case. But in case of d_path we have to do two things: call d_unlinked() and remove the suffix if it is.",
      "parentUuid": "0d7b5481_0a081c84",
